# The same drawing, where each node's touches and what it does instead are gathered into a list first (`let all = ..
# .collect()`). The list is a value of the body's own, made by the step that names it from the node, a part of the graph;
# `Touch::drawn` takes each element of the list, so what the clean side draws from the graph, the shortcut draws from a
# copy it made.

route drawing.drawn
step drawn/collect
step drawn/Touch.drawn
step drawn/Touch.drawn/Where()

line entry > drawn call
line Graph·g > drawn value
line Graph·g > drawn/collect value                            # `n.touches.iter().chain(&n.instead).collect()`
line drawn/collect > Touch·all@drawn/collect value            # `let all = ..`
line Touch·all@drawn/collect > drawn value                    # `all.into_iter()`, a call that is no step
line Touch·all@drawn/collect > drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() value
line drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() > Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() value
line Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() > drawn/Touch.drawn value
line drawn/Touch.drawn > Where@drawn/Touch.drawn value
line Where@drawn/Touch.drawn > drawn value                    # collected into the pairs the body gives back, by its own code

home Graph·g drawn
home Touch·all@drawn/collect drawn
home Where@drawn/Touch.drawn/Where() drawn/Touch.drawn
home Where@drawn/Touch.drawn drawn

side entry left
